//Part 13, The Pit: The Number of the Beast.
//The cmd line is the compiler, so it is also a calculator.

//Puts the cursor at the bottom.
Msg(MSG_KEY_DOWN,0,SC_CURSOR_DOWN|SCF_CTRL);
"\n";

TourPut(
"You have reached the bottom of Hell.  \"Let him that hath "
"understanding count the number of the beast.\"\n\n"
"The command line is the $$GREEN$$Unholy C$$FG$$ compiler, so it is "
"also a calculator.  It speaks hex, too.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"0x29A;";
InGetStr("\n");

TourPut(
"$$GREEN$$ans$$FG$$ holds the result of the last expression, in hex "
"and decimal.  $$GREEN$$0x29A$$FG$$ is 666.\n\n"
"Now the long way: add up the numbers 1 through 36.  "
"Statements run as soon as you press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"I64 n,beast_sum=0;for (n=1;n<=36;n++) beast_sum+=n;beast_sum;";
InGetStr("\n");

TourPut(
"666 again.  36 is six times six, and the numbers up to it add up "
"to the Beast.\n\n"
"Now three cubes and three sixes, with the $$GREEN$$`$$FG$$ power "
"operator.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"6`3+6`3+6`3+6+6+6;";
InGetStr("\n");

TourPut(
"$$GREEN$$ansf$$FG$$ says 666.  Looks right.  But $$GREEN$$`$$FG$$ always "
"works in floating point, and the command line only shows seven digits.  "
"Let's keep it in an integer.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"I64 beast_pow=6`3+6`3+6`3+6+6+6;beast_pow;";
InGetStr("\n");

TourPut(
"$$RED$$665!$$FG$$  The FPU really got 665.99999999999872, and the "
"conversion to an integer chopped off the rest.  That is not the "
"Number of the Beast.  That is the Neighbor of the Beast.\n\n"
"Unholy C keeps the real one in $$GREEN$$BEAST$$FG$$.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"BEAST;";
InGetStr("\n");

TourPut(
"Now see it in the scripture.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<ENTER>$$FG$$.\n");
"Ed(\"BF:Revelation,13:18\");";
InGetStr("\n");
Sleep(500);
WinToTop;//Kludge

TourPut(
"Revelation 13:18.  The Bible on this CD is the King James Version, "
"unchanged.  King Solomon's yearly gold was 666 talents, too, "
"in 1 Kings 10:14.\n\n"
"Press $$GREEN$$<SHIFT-ESC>$$FG$$ to close it.\n");
InUntilChar(CH_ESC,CH_SHIFT_ESC);

TourPut(
"That is the bottom of the pit.  The only way out is up: press "
"$$GREEN$$Ascend$$FG$$.\n",TRUE);
